# Overrides layered ON TOP OF .env for automated test runs ONLY — see package.json's
# `test` and `test:integration` scripts, which load this file SECOND via a second
# --env-file flag, so keys here win over .env for anything both files set.
#
# Why this file exists: .env now points SMTP at a real provider (Brevo) and
# ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS at real college domains, for interactive use (`npm run dev`,
# `npm start`). tests/integration/auth-flow.test.ts reads OTP codes back out of Mailpit's
# inspection API — it cannot do that against Brevo, there is no inbox to query — and
# without this override it would additionally have gone ahead and sent real email, from an
# automated test, to an address shaped like a real student ID at a real institution
# (`otp.test.<timestamp>@muj.manipal.edu`, derived from ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS). Both
# problems are fixed by making tests hermetic: local mail sink, RFC 2606 test domain,
# regardless of whatever .env currently points at for the live app.
#
# Committed (not secret) — these are all safe, non-production values by construction.

SMTP_HOST="localhost"
SMTP_PORT=1025
SMTP_USER=""
SMTP_PASSWORD=""
MAIL_FROM="Faculty Portal Tests <noreply@faculty.example.invalid>"

ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS="faculty.example.invalid"
